      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "An additional improvement would be cone detectors attached to the hands, so local object detection can happen in order to separate interaction within groups of objects.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-14T01:02:12.471Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In, the same way that we got an audio \"cone\" to hear people only from a directional point of view, is it possible that VRC can implement an \"object attractor cone\" so that it will only attempt to grab/interface with objects that are only in front of you, and not off to the side?\n\nI would really like to not have items auto highlight for interaction that are not within my visible range.\n\nIf you can make it an option with a flag, or an adjustable cone, that would be awesome. Thanks!",
